<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prīmĭtīvus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the first</i> or <i>earliest of its kind</i>,
				<i>primitive</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flores,</span>”
				<i>that blossom first</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 9,
					13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anni,</span>”
				<i>the first</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Arb. 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Gram. t. t. (for the class. primigenius, nativus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				<i>primitives</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 824</span></i>
			 P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Esp., <i>the first-born</i>: fetus, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 828: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">primitivum in pecoribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 13, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">primitivo suo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3
					Reg. 16, 34</span></i>
			.—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Asiae in Christo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Rom. 16, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
